{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790281472,"nonce":"P3+fTbig7vgXd9Y0En+hU5mNQj4=","message":"Piece 1 is done apart from one edge. 8d271ca roots each parked fiber through a VM handle slot from park until the scheduler has resumed it (slots are reused, so a per-frame game loop does not grow the handle table); before it, a fiber nothing held was swept while parked — wasm/checks/parked.wren crashes current HEAD 3/3 under node-run.mjs with 'memory access out of bounds', and passes with the fix. d988f41 moves last_module_vars_cache and wasm/src/tier_up.rs's main_module_cache onto the module's ModuleVarsCell, reading the array through it, and empties the closure-keyed cache at every collection. current_closure_cell needed nothing: it is set only for a dispatch, while the caller's frame holds the closure. The edge: a JIT'd body reads module variables through current_module_vars_cell, which holds the array pointer set at BC-\u003eJIT entry, so a body whose callee grows that module's variables mid-call keeps the old array until its next entry. Baking the module's cell address instead (as the host JIT does) would close it at one extra load per access. Pieces 2 (Immix on wasm32) and 3 (fibers for JIT'd bodies) are untouched.","files":null}]}